# netsurf: percentage and calc() heights and offsets; floated flex/grid; replaced boxes in flex
#
# - Absolutely positioned boxes with top + bottom and height auto have a
#   DEFINITE height (CSS 2.1 10.6.4), but it was only worked out after their
#   children were laid out, so every percentage height inside saw AUTO.
#   layout_absolute now settles it first and flags the box
#   (VB_DEFINITE_HEIGHT); layout_find_dimensions and min/max-height accept
#   such a containing block, and position: fixed counts as absolute there.
# - height, min-height and max-height resolve percentages and calc() through
#   css_unit_len2device_px_ref against the containing block (calc() with no
#   percentage resolves without one). top/right/bottom/left likewise, so
#   "left: calc(50% - 10px)" centres.
#   Google's consent dialog (inline-block, height: calc(100% - 64px) inside a
#   fixed top:0/bottom:0 box) was 0 px tall and invisible.
# - A floated display: flex / grid box went to layout_block_context, which
#   asserts on a grid (bbc.com, rte.ie aborted); it now gets layout_flex /
#   layout_grid like the inline variants.
# - A replaced box with given dimensions (an inline <svg>) inside a flex row
#   returned from layout_block_context with height AUTO, and
#   layout_calculate_descendant_bboxes asserted (duckduckgo.com, x.com
#   aborted): it now takes the intrinsic ratio, else square.
